  "text": "Recipe: Lentil Quinoa Uttapam | Tomato Chutney\nCreator: Sharmila Vedam\nCategory: Uttapam\nIngredients: moong dal, split urad dhal, split chana dhal, quinoa, ginger, garlic, onion, green chillies, hing (asafoetida), fruit salt, carrots, spinach, peanuts, dried red chillies, roma tomatoes, cilantro, fenugreek seeds, cumin seeds, date, curry leaves, mustard seeds, urad dal\nCooking methods: soak, blend, saute, roast\nInstructions: UTTAPAM: Soak a blend of 1 cup moong dal, 1/2 cup split urad dhal, 1/2 cup spilt chana dhal & 1.5 cups quinoa. After a few hours of soaking, blend them together with ginger, garlic, onion, green chillies, hing (asafoetida). At this point we may either let it ferment or add fruit salt and make 'Instant Uttappam'. We may optionally add chopped onion, grated carrots, spinach etc to the batter. Cook uttappam on a non-stick griddle. TOMATO CHUTNEY: 1 Tbsp dry roasted peanuts, 3-4 cloves of garlic & dried red chillies according to ur spice level, 5 small roma tomatoes, cilantro, a pinch of fenugreek seeds, a pinch of cumin seeds & 1 date. Cook till tomatoes soften. Then add dry roasted south Indian seasoning (hing, curry leaves, mustard seeds, 'urad dal').\nNotes: Instant Uttappam (made with fruit salt), South Indian seasoning (contains hing, curry leaves, mustard seeds, urad dal)",
